If the emulator reports 400 cycles, it is reporting the tile execution phase only — a partial measurement of the full pipeline. The architectural constant for the complete pipeline is 800 cycles. See §1 note on the cycle constant.

Phase 1 — Configuration Header

All magic numbers live in one place. This is the first file you write.

```c
/* st_config.h */
#ifndef ST_CONFIG_H
#define ST_CONFIG_H

/* ---- Clock ----------------------------------------------------------- */
/* F_CPU_HZ MUST match the actual core clock. A wrong value here
 * silently corrupts every timing derivation below. */
#define F_CPU_HZ            200000000UL   /* 200 MHz */

/* ---- Architectural constants ----------------------------------------- */
#define WCET_CYCLES         800           /* hard cycle budget, all platforms */
#define AET_CYCLES          680           /* measured, architectural constant  */
#define AET_NS_AT_1GHZ      800UL         /* silicon target (WCET at 1 GHz)    */

/* 64-bit arithmetic prevents integer truncation at non-round clocks.
 * Example: 480 MHz -> 1,666 ns exact (not 1,666.66 truncated to 1,666). */
#define AET_NS_AT_FCPU \
    ((uint32_t)(((uint64_t)WCET_CYCLES * 1000000000ULL) / (uint64_t)F_CPU_HZ))

/* ---- Tiles ----------------------------------------------------------- */
#define MAX_TILES           1024
#define TILE_SIZE_B         700           /* bytes per tile working set */
#define ROM_RATIO_BP        7500          /* basis points: 75.00% */
#define TILE_ROM_B          ((TILE_SIZE_B * ROM_RATIO_BP) / 10000)   /* 525 */
#define TILE_SRAM_B         (TILE_SIZE_B - TILE_ROM_B)               /* 175 */
#define TILE_UNKNOWN        0xFFFF

/* ---- FIS triage ------------------------------------------------------ */
/* Size of the FIS rule table, in entries (uint16_t each).
 * 4096 entries = 8 KB in ROM. Must be a power of two for cheap modulo. */
#define FIS_TABLE_SIZE      4096

/* ---- Error codes ----------------------------------------------------- */
#define ERR_NONE            0x0000
#define ERR_AMBIG           0xAB16
#define ERR_WCET            0x0C37
#define ERR_TILE            0x7113
#define ERR_UPDATE          0x0D9E

#endif /* ST_CONFIG_H */
```

Memory reconciliation. 1024 tiles × 700 B = 700 KB total tile data. This lives in flash (2–4 MB is more than sufficient). At runtime, only one tile's 700-byte working set is resident in SRAM. The 1 MB SRAM requirement covers the active tile, the FSM state, the ternary scratch buffers, and the stack.

