5. Platform Notes

5.1 ARM Cortex-M7 (STM32H7, i.MX RT1024)

```c
/* Configure DTCM/ITCM for deterministic execution.
 * Do NOT enable D-cache for the ST-T1024 hot path: it makes WCET
 * analysis intractable on this class of core. */
SCB_EnableICache();          /* I-cache is fine: code is fixed */
/* SCB_EnableDCache(); */    /* deliberately NOT enabled */
```

Place the FSM, ternary scratch buffers, and the active tile in DTCM (address 0x20000000 on STM32H7). DTCM has fixed single-cycle access — deterministic by construction.

MPU regions (use CMSIS ARM_MPU_SetRegion):

Region Base Size Access
ROM (tiles) 0x08000000 4 MB read-only
DTCM (active tile) 0x20000000 128 KB read-write
Stack guard 0x2001F000 4 KB no-access

5.2 RISC-V NEORV32

Add the ternary dot product as a custom instruction. This is the single highest-leverage change you can make: it collapses the hot loop into one opcode.

```c
/* Custom opcode 0x0B, funct3 = 0 */
static inline int32_t ternary_dot_insn(uint32_t ap, uint32_t an,
                                       uint32_t bp, uint32_t bn) {
    int32_t r;
    __asm__ volatile (
        ".insn r 0x0B, 0x0, 0x0, %0, %1, %2"
        : "=r"(r)
        : "r"(ap), "r"(an), "r"(bp), "r"(bn)
    );
    return r;
}
```

5.3 PULPino

Single-core RV32, open-source, well-supported by the PULP toolchain. Adequate for SIL 2-level prototypes. Use the event unit for deterministic interrupt latency.

