10. Agentic Deployments

This guide covers base ST-T1024 — the inference architecture. For deployments requiring verifiable agency — action libraries, plan libraries, trajectory predicates, and inter-organizational admission — see:

AGENTIC ST-T1024 CASE STUDY: ADAPTIVE CRUISE CONTROL Version2

The agentic extension adds:

· A finite, ROM-burned action library
· A finite, ROM-burned plan library with three policies (HALT, ROLLBACK, ESCALATE)
· A trajectory predicate layer that catches sequence-level hazards no per-action contract can see
· The A11–A16 inter-organizational layer for cross-org admission

The MCU implementation described here is the substrate for the agentic layer. Both are certified against the same architecture.

