Appendix B — Pedagogical Traps (for instructors)

Version 1.0 of this guide contained four deliberate faults, preserved in v2.1 behind a build flag so the default build is a working reference.

```c
#ifdef ENABLE_PEDAGOGY_TRAPS
  /* TRAP 1: unit confusion */
  #define WCET_CYCLES 800   /* comment says "in ns" — student must notice */
#else
  #define WCET_CYCLES 800   /* in cycles */
#endif
```


To use the traps in a course:

1. Compile with -DENABLE_PEDAGOGY_TRAPS
2. Do not tell students which lines are traps
3. Grade on whether they find all four

# Trap Lesson General principle
1 #define WCET_CYCLES 800 /* in ns */ Cycles ≠ nanoseconds Every number has a unit
2 #define TILE_SIZE_KB 700 (× 1024 = 716 MB) Order-of-magnitude Every multiplication has a scale
3 SCB_EnableDCache() in init Cache breaks WCET Every timing claim has a memory-model assumption
4 pdMS_TO_TICKS(1) for an 800 ns task RTOS tick granularity Every schedule has a granularity
5 acc += __builtin_popcount(x) on Cortex-M7 No hardware popcount Every intrinsic has a hardware assumption

"Pedagogy is a gap the reader knows is intentional; a bug is a gap the reader assumes is accidental."

